<title>USA: House panel to act on U.S. airline ticket tax.</title>
<headline>House panel to act on U.S. airline ticket tax.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The House Ways and Means Committee Friday scheduled a meeting next Wednesday to act on a bill to reinstate the 10 percent airline ticket tax that expired at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>The Senate Finance Committee approved the bill this Wednesday. The bill also gives the Treasury Department authority to transfer $1.2 billion in tax revenues collected by the airlines last year, but not sent to the Treasury until last month after the tax lapsed.</p>
</text>
